\description{
The first weekly wave of the Democracy Fund + UCLA Nationscape survey,
fielded July 18–24, 2019. Approximately 6,250 completed online interviews
drawn from the Lucid respondent exchange platform using a non-probability
quota design, with raking weights calibrated to ACS demographic targets
and 2016 presidential vote choice.
}
\details{
This dataset is the first of 77 weekly waves collected from July 2019
through January 2021. The full survey ran in three phases:\tabular{llll}{
   Phase \tab Weeks \tab Dates \tab Approx. N \cr
   Phase 1 \tab 1–24 \tab Jul 18, 2019 – Dec 26, 2019 \tab 150,000 \cr
   Phase 2 \tab 25–50 \tab Jan 2, 2020 – Jun 25, 2020 \tab 162,500 \cr
   Phase 3 \tab 51–77 \tab Jul 2, 2020 – Jan 12, 2021 \tab 168,750 \cr
}


Only Wave 1 is bundled in the package because 77 waves × ~6,250 rows
would be prohibitively large. To obtain the full dataset by phase, use the
prepare scripts in \verb{data-raw/} (see the Source section).

\strong{Survey design:}
The Nationscape is a calibrated non-probability sample (quota design with
raking weights). Use \code{\link[=as_survey_nonprob]{as_survey_nonprob()}} — it is designed specifically
for this use case and will gain bootstrap re-calibration variance in Phase
2.5:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{svy <- as_survey_nonprob(ns_wave1, weights = weight)
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

\strong{Metadata:}
All substantive columns carry variable labels (\code{"label"} attribute) set
during data preparation. Battery items additionally carry a
\code{"question_preface"} attribute with the shared question stem. Value
labels (\code{"labels"} attribute) are present for all coded response items.

\strong{Battery structure:}
Most multi-item question groups follow a \verb{\{battery\}_\{item\}} naming
convention. All items within a battery share an identical
\code{"question_preface"} attribute:\tabular{lll}{
   Battery prefix \tab Preface summary \tab N items \cr
   \verb{news_sources_*} \tab News sources used in past week \tab 13 \cr
   \verb{group_favorability_*} \tab Favorability toward named groups \tab 13 \cr
   \verb{cand_favorability_*} \tab Favorability toward named candidates \tab 9 \cr
   \verb{trump_*} \tab Trump head-to-head matchups \tab 10 \cr
   \verb{pence_*} \tab Pence head-to-head matchups \tab 5 \cr
   \verb{cand_truth_*} \tab Whether each candidate tells the truth \tab 6 \cr
   \verb{cand_facts_*} \tab Whether each candidate relies on facts \tab 6 \cr
   \verb{racial_attitudes_*} \tab Agree/disagree racial attitude items \tab 4 \cr
   \verb{gender_attitudes_*} \tab Agree/disagree gender attitude items \tab 4 \cr
   \verb{discrimination_*} \tab Perceived discrimination by group \tab 6 \cr
}


Three policy batteries share the same Agree/Disagree/Neither scale:
\code{wall}, \code{cap_carbon}, \code{environment}, \code{guns_bg}, \code{mctaxes}, \code{estate_tax},
\code{raise_upper_tax}, \code{college}, \code{abortion_waiting}, \code{abortion_never},
